WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.440
Did our species begin in one place, on one date?

2
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.200
A skull from Jebel Irhoud, in Morocco, seems to answer yes.

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.320
It comes with a date that looks precise.

4
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.690
It has a face you could pass in the street.

5
00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.390
Its braincase is more elongated than yours.

6
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.290
It is a mosaic of modern and older features.

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.480
Now ask the question that runs through this whole lesson.

8
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.880
What was actually dated?

9
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.140
Not the skull itself.

10
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.620
Flints lay beside the bones, and a fire had heated them.

11
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.760
Enough heat resets the flint's signal.

12
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.060
Afterward, radiation from the flint and its surroundings builds it back.

13
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.400
The stored dose, divided by the yearly dose, gives the time since heating.

14
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.020
So this date belongs to something beside the bones, not to the bones themselves.

15
00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.740
Every date in this story needs that same check.

16
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.890
Travel east to Omo, in Ethiopia.

17
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.170
Here a fossil lies in one layer, and a band of volcanic ash lies above it.

18
00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:14.850
The eruption that laid the ash has been dated too.

19
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.760
The ash lies above the bone, and the date belongs to the ash.

20
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.400
So is the bone older or younger than that date?

21
00:01:29.867 --> 00:01:34.287
At least as old. The ash fell after the bone was buried.

22
00:01:35.547 --> 00:01:36.847
So its date is a minimum.

23
00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:41.527
Omo I is at least about that old, not dated directly.

24
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:44.670
Now cross into western Asia.

25
00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:50.350
At Misliya Cave, in Israel, a jaw with teeth from our lineage turned up.

26
00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:55.310
It was dated far earlier than the dispersal many textbooks taught.

27
00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.430
Part of that dating has been challenged.

28
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.220
Does that mean living people outside Africa descend from them?

29
00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:09.000
Not by itself. A fossil shows presence, not ancestry.

30
00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:14.700
Genomes of living non-Africans point mainly to a later dispersal.

31
00:02:15.683 --> 00:02:17.863
So the dates do not mark one birthplace.

32
00:02:19.223 --> 00:02:23.543
People with partly modern anatomy lived in north Africa very early.

33
00:02:24.803 --> 00:02:27.743
They lived in east Africa by at least the Omo date.

34
00:02:28.817 --> 00:02:33.977
Genomes of living people agree that most of our ancestry traces to Africa.

35
00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:37.797
But the history is not one tree with one root.

36
00:02:38.997 --> 00:02:43.017
It is connected populations that split, and sometimes merged again.

37
00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:48.607
So whenever you meet a date in this story, ask two plain questions before you

38
00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:51.007
believe it. What was dated?

39
00:02:52.327 --> 00:02:53.167
And where did it lie?
